  description: Magnesium is a chemical element with symbol Mg and atomic number 12.
    It is a shiny gray solid which bears a close physical resemblance to the other
    five elements in the second column (Group 2, or alkaline earth metals) of the
    periodic table:they each have the same electron configuration in their outer
    electron shell producing a similar crystal structure. Magnesium is the ninth
    most abundant element in the universe.
